### policies/policies/github-read-only.yaml  [code]
- id: github-readonly
- name: GitHub — read only
- description: >
-   Read access to issues, pull requests, repositories, and code search.
-   Creating issues and adding comments requires approval.
-   No destructive actions permitted.
- rules:
-   # Read operations — always allowed
-   - service: github
-   - service: github
-     actions: [list_issues, get_issue, list_prs, get_pr, list_repos, search_code]
-     allow: true
-   # Write operations — require approval
-     actions: [create_issue, comment_issue]
-     require_approval: true
-     reason: Creating issues and comments requires your approval

### policies/policies/google-workspace-safe.yaml  [code]
- id: google-workspace-safe
- name: Google Workspace — safe defaults
- description: >
-   Read-only access to Gmail, Calendar, Drive, and Contacts.
-   Write operations (send email, create/modify events and files) require human approval.
-   Destructive actions (delete email) are blocked.
- rules:
-   # Gmail — read operations allowed, send requires approval, delete blocked
-   - service: google.gmail
-   - service: google.gmail
-   - service: google.gmail
-     actions: [list_messages, get_message]
-     allow: true
-     allow: true
-     allow: true
-     allow: true
-     actions: [send_message, create_draft]
-     require_approval: true
-     require_approval: true
-     require_approval: true
-     reason: Sending email requires your approval
-     actions: [delete_message]
-     allow: false
-     reason: Email deletion is disabled for safety
-   # Calendar — read allowed, write requires approval
-   - service: google.calendar
-   - service: google.calendar
-     actions: [list_events, get_event, list_calendars]
-     actions: [create_event, update_event, delete_event]
-     reason: Calendar changes require your approval
-   # Drive — read and preview allowed, write requires approval
-   - service: google.drive
-   - service: google.drive
-     actions: [list_files, get_file, search_files]
-     actions: [create_file, update_file]
-     reason: File creation and editing require your approval
-   # Contacts — read-only
-   - service: google.contacts
-     actions: [list_contacts, get_contact, search_contacts]

### policies/policies/imessage-safe-default.yaml  [code]
- id: imessage-safe-default
- name: iMessage — read only (default)
- description: >
-   Read-only access to iMessage conversations.
-   Sending messages is explicitly blocked and requires a policy change to enable.
-   Even with an allow policy, send_message ALWAYS requires human approval at request time.
- rules:
-   # Read operations — allowed
-   - service: apple.imessage
-   - service: apple.imessage
-     actions: [search_messages, list_threads, get_thread]
-     allow: true
-   # Sending — blocked by default; must be explicitly enabled and always requires approval
-     actions: [send_message]
-     allow: false
-     reason: >
-       Sending iMessages is disabled by default.
-       To enable it, change this rule to require_approval: true.
-       Note: send_message always requires human approval regardless of policy.